<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Dorbyl raises half yr shr, div unchanged.</title>
<headline>Dorbyl raises half yr shr, div unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     244.9	 vs   194.7</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  60.0	 vs    60.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   103.79	vs    67.10</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   136.03	vs    99.42</p>
<p>    Tax			  33.06	vs    31.34</p>
<p>    Turnover		1,758.91	vs 1,650.49</p>
<p>Div payable around January 10 1997</p>
<p>on register December 6 1996</p>
<p>Full name:  Dorbyl Ltd (industrial-engineering)</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said it continued to focus on exports and the development of new niche markets. Accordingly, the need to be internationally competitive has been given a high priority and significant resources are being allocated to improving information technology throughout the group.</p>
<p>Benefits flowing from these improved systems are expected in the latter half of 1997.</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts forecast earnings per share edging up to between 234.2 and 246.0 with consensus at 240.7 cents and a dividend of 35.5 cents .</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
